    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s May 29th slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.43) stands as our clear anchor, offering the highest utility score against a middling Samaniego. While he faces a lefty, his elite contact profile overrides any platoon concerns, making him our primary engine for production. We also see high-ceiling value in **Matt Chapman** (69.89) and **Luis Arraez** (66.78), both benefiting from a soft matchup against Lorenzen. With an favorable park factor (+14%) and optimal lineup placement, this trio is positioned to carry our offensive output today. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.58) also rounds out a strong core; despite a slight park penalty, his favorable platoon split against Ure\u00f1a keeps him in the high-60s range, making him an essential start.\n\nIn terms of bench decisions, **Bryson Stott** (44.95) was the most difficult exclusion. While his projected score hovered near our utility threshold, he was ultimately edged out due to a difficult matchup against Wrobleski and the restrictive platoon penalty associated with facing a lefty. We preferred the park-adjusted upside of **Daulton Varsho** (57.38) and **Taylor Ward** (59.46) to fill our final outfield slots. We remain particularly cautious regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Lawrence Butler**. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** still sidelined on the IL, our catching depth remains thin; should **Will Smith** be held out of the lineup entirely, we will have to pivot quickly to maintain our production floor. \n\nInvestors should monitor the wind and weather reports closely for the **Taylor Ward** matchup; despite facing a tough arm in Macko, the combination of a +16% park factor and the leadoff spot makes him a high-leverage play. Conversely, **Masyn Winn** (46.94) and **Lawrence Butler** (50.41) represent our lowest-ceiling starts of the day due to their respective matchups against Imanaga and Rod\u00f3n. We are keeping **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Bryson Stott** ready on the bench as immediate contingency options should late-breaking lineup changes force us to shift away from the current starters.",
